### =============================================
### SIGN IN
### Si se incluye orgId, el JWT lleva roles acotados a esa org.
### Sin orgId, el token usa los roles globales del usuario.
### El script guarda el token automáticamente en {{auth_token}}.
### =============================================

### Login global (sin org activa)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/auth/signin
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "admin",
  "password": "admin123"
}

> {% client.global.set("auth_token", response.body.token); %}

###

### Login admin con org activa → roles de org 1 (TechCorp)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/auth/signin
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "admin",
  "password": "admin123",
  "orgId": 1
}

> {% client.global.set("auth_token", response.body.token); %}

